  "proof": [
    "The parent graph encloses every possible radiative pair in every refinement. Ground is an unsplit centre, roof support is the closed polygon. The 15 m radius exceeds the furthest parent-centre distance for any directly contacting 5 m ground squares.",
    "For one direct ignition footprint on one retained ordinary roof, all reachable potential components of every surviving patch bearing that owner are included. Given positive covered area, selecting more patches or more components only enlarges the bound.",
    "An independent universal thermal certificate allows protected parents to be removed from the propagation graph. Additional clearing removes external fuels, so the same contact and accumulated energy inequalities still hold. Empirically screened alternatives retain all core parents when computing the bound.",
    "The number bound unions original roof owners across included components, adds unrepresented original owners, and includes failed identity claims conservatively. The area uses physical covered fuel area after clearing.",
    "The bounds assume the closed frozen domain, no imposed fire entering later from outside, no spotting, no active ignition on a cleared patch, and one ordinary roof as the only source. They measure maximum possible modeled losses, not observed losses."
  ],
